---
import CopyCommand from "../components/CopyCommand.astro";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Pigeon docs"
  description="Install and configure Pigeon for your coding agents."
  active="docs"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-28 pt-36 sm:pt-44">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-light tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">Set up Pigeon</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-500">
      Pigeon creates a Cloudflare R2 bucket, configures upload access, and installs a shared agent
      skill.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-14 space-y-14">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-neutral-200">1. Create a Cloudflare token</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-7 text-neutral-500">
          Pigeon needs one Cloudflare API token that carries two permissions: <strong
            class="text-neutral-300">Workers R2 Storage · Edit</strong
          > (creates the bucket, public route, and lifecycle rule) and <strong
            class="text-neutral-300">API Tokens · Write</strong
          > (mints the bucket-scoped upload key). The token is never stored.
        </p>
        <ol class="mt-4 max-w-2xl space-y-2 text-sm leading-7 text-neutral-500">
          <li>
            1. Open <a
              href="https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens"
              class="text-neutral-300 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-white"
              >dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens</a
            >.
          </li>
          <li>2. Click <strong class="text-neutral-300">Create Token</strong>.</li>
          <li>
            3. At the bottom, next to <strong class="text-neutral-300">Create Custom Token</strong>,
            click <strong class="text-neutral-300">Get started</strong>.
          </li>
          <li>4. Name it <code class="text-neutral-300">p1geon</code>.</li>
          <li>
            5. Under <strong class="text-neutral-300">Permissions</strong>, set the first row to <code
              class="text-neutral-300">Account → Workers R2 Storage → Edit</code
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            6. Click <strong class="text-neutral-300">+ Add more</strong> and set the second row to <code
              class="text-neutral-300">User → API Tokens → Write</code
            >.
          </li>
          <li>
            7. Under <strong class="text-neutral-300">Account Resources</strong>, choose <code
              class="text-neutral-300">Include</code
            > → your account.
          </li>
          <li>
            8. Click <strong class="text-neutral-300">Continue to summary</strong>, then <strong
              class="text-neutral-300">Create Token</strong
            >, and copy the token — it is shown only once.
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-7 text-neutral-500">
          Find your <strong class="text-neutral-300">Account ID</strong> on the R2 Overview page (right
          sidebar), or in the dashboard URL after <code class="text-neutral-300"
            >dash.cloudflare.com/</code
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-neutral-200">2. Run setup</h2>
        <div class="mt-4">
          <CopyCommand command="p1geon init --account YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID" />
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-neutral-500">
          Paste the token when prompted (or set <code class="text-neutral-300"
            >CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN</code
          >). Add <code class="text-neutral-300">--dry-run</code> to validate the token and account without
          creating anything. To supply pre-made bucket credentials instead, add <code
            class="text-neutral-300">--with-key</code
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-neutral-200">3. Check it works</h2>
        <div class="mt-4">
          <CopyCommand command="p1geon doctor" />
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-neutral-500">
          Doctor uploads a small file, opens it through the public route, then deletes it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-white/[0.06] pt-10">
        <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-neutral-200">Requirements</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-neutral-500">
          Agents use <code class="text-neutral-300">aws-cli</code> to upload files. Screenshot capture
          uses native tools or headless Chromium. Config lives at <code class="text-neutral-300"
            >~/.pigeon/config</code
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-neutral-200">Manage it</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-2 font-mono text-sm text-neutral-400">
          <p>p1geon env --shell sh</p>
          <p>p1geon rotate</p>
          <p>p1geon destroy</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
